  "sport": "floorball",
  "title": "The wheel – passing on the move",
  "description": "Four players form a ring, about seven metres across, and a fifth player (X) stands in the middle. The players in the ring keep moving forwards around it. Whoever has the ball passes in to X, who plays it out to the next player in the ring.\n\nVariations: the players in the ring move backwards, or the other way round so they have to pass on the backhand. Change the middle player after a while. With more players: build two wheels. The diagram is not to scale.",
  "coachingPoints": [
    {
      "id": "cp1",
      "text": "Receive and pass without stopping."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp2",
      "text": "X: turn towards the next player before the ball arrives."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp3",
      "text": "Pass in front of the moving player, not behind them."
    }
  ],
